        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 174,
        "headingId": 433,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8850/0 Lipoma, NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:16:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 477,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 434,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67654,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 174,
        "headingId": 434,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2E80.0 &amp; XH1PL8 Lipoma &amp; Lipoma, NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:16:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 478,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 435,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67655,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 174,
        "headingId": 435,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:16:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 479,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 436,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67656,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 174,
        "headingId": 436,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:16:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 480,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 437,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67657,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 174,
        "headingId": 437,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Intrathoracic lipomas may be located in any compartment of the mediastinum {26358059}, diaphragm {17532428; 9663548}, bronchus {19395910; 24121172; 12527636; 8008745}, lung {3731900}, or chest wall {13429696; 18573434}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:16:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 481,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 438,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67658,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 174,
        "headingId": 438,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Although most intrathoracic lipomas are asymptomatic, patients may occasionally present with cough, dyspnoea, heart failure, or even death {18573434}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:16:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 482,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 439,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67659,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 174,
        "headingId": 439,
        "headingText": "<p>Intrathoracic lipomas are rare, most frequently reported in the mediastinum as thymolipomas (see <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/35/175\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Thymolipoma</em>) and chest wall; they account for 1&ndash;9% of primary thymic masses {26358059}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-02-23T18:10:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 483,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 440,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67660,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 174,
        "headingId": 440,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:16:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 484,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 441,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67661,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 174,
        "headingId": 441,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Translocations involving 12q13-q15, resulting in fusion of <em>HMGA2</em> with a variety of gene partners, are the most common alterations and drive the pathogenesis of lipomas. Other reported chromosomal abnormalities include 6p and 13q rearrangements {9530339; 24121172}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:16:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 491,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 448,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67662,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 174,
        "headingId": 448,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Lipomas are well-circumscribed tumours with a uniform glistening yellow to pale-tan cut surface.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:16:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 485,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 442,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67663,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 174,
        "headingId": 442,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The majority of intrathoracic lipomas are composed predominantly of mature adipose tissue, with limited variability in adipocyte size. Occasionally, myxoid change or areas of fibrosis are present. Scattered atypical spindled or multinucleated cells can be appreciated in endobronchial lipomas, but evidence suggests that these tumours share molecular characteristics with lipomas at other sites {19395910; 1948801; 24121172}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:16:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 486,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 443,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67664,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 174,
        "headingId": 443,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Aspiration specimens show adipocytes containing a single large lipid droplet with a compressed rim of cytoplasm and a flattened inconspicuous nucleus.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:16:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 487,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 444,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67665,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 174,
        "headingId": 444,
        "headingText": "<p>Diagnostic molecular pathology is not usually required. In large tumours (&gt;&nbsp;100 mm) and/or tumours with cytological atypia, exclusion of <em>MDM2</em> amplification may be helpful to exclude well-differentiated liposarcoma {17895748; 18500263; 26146760; 16160477}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-02-01T10:26:09"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 490,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 447,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67666,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 174,
        "headingId": 447,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Mature uniform adipocytes without cytological atypia</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Absence of <em>MDM2</em> amplification in large tumours and/or cases with cytological atypia</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:16:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 488,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 445,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67667,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 174,
        "headingId": 445,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:16:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 489,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 446,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67668,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 174,
        "headingId": 446,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Intrathoracic lipomas are benign, with recurrence rates of &lt;&nbsp;5% {18573434; 24121172}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:16:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]